\inactive makes the editor pane it is executed in
inactive. It takes no arguments:

\inactive

When a pane is inactive, executing lines in it does
nothing. The only line that is still executed is a line
that contains only \active (without any indentation or
other text), which makes the pane active again:

\active

This is useful to prevent code in a pane from being
executed by accident. The setting concerns only the pane
where the command is executed.
